WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.091 --> 00:00:08.773
<v Daniel>You know, if you were to walk into a room full of tech CEOs today and just ask them if we're on the verge of a runaway intelligence explosion.</v>

2
00:00:08.953 --> 00:00:09.953
<v Maya>Oh, they all say yes.</v>

3
00:00:10.273 --> 00:00:21.676
<v Daniel>Right. They would look you right in the eye and say, absolutely. You know, that whole sci-fi moment where AI gets smart enough to improve its own code and progress just instantly skyrockets to infinity.</v>

4
00:00:21.776 --> 00:00:25.857
<v Maya>Yeah, the singularity. It's all anyone talks about.</v>

5
00:00:26.125 --> 00:00:38.596
<v Daniel>Exactly. But if you look at the actual mathematical threshold required for a machine to infinitely improve itself. We aren't even close. Let's be real. We are actually failing the test right now by six percentage points.</v>

6
00:00:38.676 --> 00:00:47.561
<v Maya>Which is such a sobering reality check, honestly. I mean, for years, this entire debate around runaway AI has been completely dominated by philosophical arguments.</v>

7
